      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Ray sends cache to one worker and router to the other. Trace is waiting. Cache needs four ticks. Router needs two. Watch router finish. Worker two picks up trace. Three more ticks and all three results are ready at five. With one worker they'd finish at nine. The ledger counts three. The driver holds a handle for each result. Now the process that kept count exits. Its replacement starts with the constructor shown here. What count will it report?",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 32.665,
          "duration": 32.265,
          "until": 35.065
        },
        {
          "say": "Zero. The old process kept the count in memory. Look at router. A worker already computed that pair of numbers. The driver owns the handle for the result, and the driver is still alive.",
          "start": 35.065,
          "end": 48.72,
          "duration": 13.655,
          "until": 49.519999999999996
        },
        {
          "say": "Give the new ledger those same three handles in one call. Ray delivers the three values to it. The ledger counts them and we're back at three. That ledger is a Ray actor. Each call goes to an instance that can remember what the last call did.",
          "start": 49.519999999999996,
          "end": 64.77499999999999,
          "duration": 15.255,
          "until": 65.775
        }
      ],
